From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] RedfishConfigHandler: quiesce the Redfish stack at ReadyToBoot

Hot-unplugging the NIC that carries the Redfish service is fatal after the
feature drivers have bound to it. Observed on RPi5 (2026-08-17) with the
BMC's USB CDC-NCM gadget re-enumerating while the user sat in Setup:

  UsbBusDxe detach -> DisconnectController cascade (NetworkCommon, Snp,
  Mnp, Arp, Ip4, Tcp teardown) -> destroying RedfishDiscoverDxe's TCP4
  probe child re-enters its Stop(), which DisconnectControllers the
  discover-protocol handle mid-cascade -> RedfishConfigDriverBindingStop
  sweeps every registered EDKII_REDFISH_CONFIG_HANDLER's Stop() -> each
  RedfishClientPkg feature driver calls RedfishCleanupService() on a
  service whose HTTP child died earlier in the same cascade ->
  HttpIoDestroyIo's Http->Configure(Http, NULL) branches through the freed
  EFI_HTTP_PROTOCOL instance:

    Synchronous Exception at 0xAFAFAFAFAFAFAFAF   (DEBUG freed-pool fill)
    X0 = stale Http pointer, X1 = 0 (NULL config), X2 = 0xAF.. fn pointer

The feature drivers hold their HTTP/REST EX references without driver-model
opens, so the handle database cannot order the teardown for them.

Fix: register a ReadyToBoot handler that stops every config handler while
the transport is still fully alive (RedfishCleanupService then runs against
valid protocol instances and NULLs the service pointers - the handlers'
Stop() is idempotent, so the later sweep from a real disconnect cascade
finds nothing to free), and latch gRedfishConfigQuiesced so that the
config-handler driver never initializes handlers or re-acquires services
past that point. Setup and boot loaders always run after ReadyToBoot
(EfiBootManagerBoot signals it before StartImage), so the whole
in-Setup hot-unplug window is covered; the BIOS-side Redfish exchange is
over by then by design. The latch also keeps the cached
gEfiRedfishDiscoverProtocol from being dereferenced when a re-enumerated
NIC reinstalls the discover protocol after its old instance was freed.

Upstream-Status: Submittable [generic RedfishPkg lifecycle fix]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.c b/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.c
index f6c8c3d..0f75ace 100644
--- a/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.c
+++ b/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.c
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ REDFISH_CONFIG_DRIVER_DATA  gRedfishConfigData;     // Only one Redfish service
 EFI_EVENT                          gEndOfDxeEvent        = NULL;
 EFI_EVENT                          gExitBootServiceEvent = NULL;
 EDKII_REDFISH_CREDENTIAL_PROTOCOL  *gCredential          = NULL;
+EFI_EVENT                          gReadyToBootEvent     = NULL;
+BOOLEAN                            gRedfishConfigQuiesced = FALSE;
 
 /**
   Callback function executed when the EndOfDxe event group is signaled.
@@ -45,6 +47,50 @@ RedfishConfigOnEndOfDxe (
   gEndOfDxeEvent = NULL;
 }
 
+/**
+  Callback function executed when the ReadyToBoot event group is signaled.
+
+  Stops every registered Redfish config handler while the network stack that
+  carries their Redfish services is still fully connected, and latches
+  gRedfishConfigQuiesced so discovery and configuration cannot restart.
+
+  Past ReadyToBoot the platform is in Setup, a boot loader, or the OS; the
+  BIOS-side Redfish exchange is over. Leaving services alive here is what
+  made a hot-unplug of the underlying NIC fatal (observed with a BMC USB
+  network gadget re-enumerating while the user sat in Setup, RPi5
+  2026-08-17): the DisconnectController cascade destroys the HTTP and REST
+  EX instances first, then reaches RedfishConfigDriverBindingStop, whose
+  handler sweep makes each feature driver call RedfishCleanupService over
+  the freed transport - ending in Http->Configure through freed pool
+  (0xAFAFAFAFAFAFAFAF fill). Stopping the handlers now runs the same
+  cleanup while every protocol instance is still valid, and the later
+  sweep from the disconnect cascade finds only NULLed services.
+
+  @param[in]   Event    Event whose notification function is being invoked.
+  @param[out]  Context  Pointer to the Context buffer.
+
+**/
+VOID
+EFIAPI
+RedfishConfigOnReadyToBoot (
+  IN  EFI_EVENT  Event,
+  OUT VOID       *Context
+  )
+{
+  EFI_STATUS  Status;
+
+  gRedfishConfigQuiesced = TRUE;
+
+  Status = RedfishConfigCommonStop ();
+  DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "%a: Redfish config handlers stopped at ReadyToBoot - %r\n", __func__, Status));
+
+  //
+  // Close event, so it will not be invoked again.
+  //
+  gBS->CloseEvent (gReadyToBootEvent);
+  gReadyToBootEvent = NULL;
+}
+
 /**
   Callback function executed when the ExitBootService event group is signaled.
 
@@ -90,6 +136,11 @@ RedfishConfigDriverCommonUnload (
     gExitBootServiceEvent = NULL;
   }
 
+  if (gReadyToBootEvent != NULL) {
+    gBS->CloseEvent (gReadyToBootEvent);
+    gReadyToBootEvent = NULL;
+  }
+
   if (gRedfishConfigData.Event != NULL) {
     gBS->CloseEvent (gRedfishConfigData.Event);
     gRedfishConfigData.Event = NULL;
@@ -160,6 +211,25 @@ RedfishConfigCommonInit (
     return Status;
   }
 
+  //
+  // Create ReadyToBoot event to stop the Redfish config handlers while the
+  // network transport underneath their services is still alive.
+  //
+  Status = EfiCreateEventReadyToBootEx (
+             TPL_CALLBACK,
+             RedfishConfigOnReadyToBoot,
+             NULL,
+             &gReadyToBootEvent
+             );
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    gBS->CloseEvent (gEndOfDxeEvent);
+    gEndOfDxeEvent = NULL;
+    gBS->CloseEvent (gExitBootServiceEvent);
+    gExitBootServiceEvent = NULL;
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "%a: Fail to register Ready To Boot event.", __func__));
+    return Status;
+  }
+
   return EFI_SUCCESS;
 }
 
diff --git a/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.h b/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.h
index 203b394..0ff78a3 100644
--- a/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.h
+++ b/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerCommon.h
@@ -46,6 +46,15 @@ typedef struct {
   REDFISH_CONFIG_SERVICE_INFORMATION    RedfishServiceInfo; /// Redfish Service information discovered
 } REDFISH_CONFIG_DRIVER_DATA;
 
+//
+// TRUE once ReadyToBoot has fired and the registered Redfish config handlers
+// have been stopped. Redfish discovery and configuration must not restart
+// past this point: the network stack underneath any Redfish service can now
+// be torn down at any time (OS driver takeover, device hot-unplug), and the
+// handlers would then free services over dead transports.
+//
+extern BOOLEAN  gRedfishConfigQuiesced;
+
 /**
   Common code of unloading image for both UEFI/DXE Redfish Configuration drivers.
 
diff --git a/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerDriver.c b/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerDriver.c
index d6498b5..3b166a8 100644
--- a/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerDriver.c
+++ b/RedfishPkg/RedfishConfigHandler/RedfishConfigHandlerDriver.c
@@ -77,6 +77,14 @@ RedfishConfigHandlerInstalledCallback (
   IN VOID       *Context
   )
 {
+  if (gRedfishConfigQuiesced) {
+    //
+    // Past ReadyToBoot: do not initialize config handlers over a network
+    // stack that can be torn down at any time from here on.
+    //
+    return;
+  }
+
   if (!gRedfishDiscoverActivated) {
     //
     // No Redfish service is discovered yet.
@@ -313,9 +321,11 @@ RedfishServiceDiscoveredCallback (
   gBS->CloseEvent (RedfishDiscoveredToken->Event);
 
   //
-  // Only support one Redfish service on platform.
+  // Only support one Redfish service on platform. Ignore services that
+  // complete discovery after ReadyToBoot: their transport is no longer
+  // guaranteed to outlive the handlers that would bind to them.
   //
-  if (!gRedfishServiceDiscovered) {
+  if (!gRedfishConfigQuiesced && !gRedfishServiceDiscovered) {
     RedfishInstance = RedfishDiscoveredToken->DiscoverList.RedfishInstances;
     //
     // Only pick up the first found Redfish service.
@@ -363,6 +373,13 @@ AcquireRedfishServiceOnNetworkInterfaceCallback (
   UINTN                                   NetworkInterfaceIndex;
   EFI_REDFISH_DISCOVERED_TOKEN            *ThisRedfishDiscoveredToken;
 
+  if (gRedfishConfigQuiesced) {
+    //
+    // Past ReadyToBoot: do not start new Redfish service discovery.
+    //
+    return;
+  }
+
   ThisNetworkInterface = mNetworkInterfaces;
   //
   // Loop to discover Redfish service on each network interface.
@@ -440,6 +457,16 @@ RedfishDiscoverProtocolInstalled (
   EFI_HANDLE  HandleBuffer;
   VOID        *RedfishHostInterfaceReadyProtocol;
 
+  if (gRedfishConfigQuiesced) {
+    //
+    // Past ReadyToBoot: a re-installed discover protocol means the NIC was
+    // hot-unplugged and rebuilt (BMC USB gadget re-enumeration). Do not
+    // re-acquire: the cached gEfiRedfishDiscoverProtocol may point into the
+    // torn-down instance, and no configuration runs past this point anyway.
+    //
+    return;
+  }
+
   DEBUG ((DEBUG_MANAGEABILITY, "%a: New network interface is installed on system by EFI Redfish discover driver.\n", __func__));
 
   BufferSize = sizeof (EFI_HANDLE);
